                <h2 class="section-title">What Is OPC Registration?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Incorporating a One Person Company under S2(62) via SPICe+ with RoC Delhi. Single member (sole director possible) + nominee (INC-3). Private limited with simplified compliance. For <a href="#">DSC</a> (needed for filing), see our page.</p>
                    <p>Post-April 2021: no turnover/capital limit for mandatory conversion. NRIs with 120 days eligible. No AGM, no cash flow statement, 2 board meetings vs 4. For <a href="/gst-registration/gurugram">GST Registration Gurugram</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for OPC Registration:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>S2(62):</strong> Companies Act 2013. OPC = private limited with single member + nominee</li><li><strong>No Limit:</strong> April 2021 removed Rs 50L capital / Rs 2 Cr turnover conversion. Grow unlimited</li><li><strong>Nominee:</strong> Standby via INC-3. Takes over on death/incapacity. Indian citizen, resident. Changeable</li><li><strong>Simplified:</strong> No AGM. No cash flow. 2 board meetings/year. AOC-4 + MGT-7A (simplified)</li><li><strong>NRI Eligible:</strong> 120 days India residency in preceding FY. Indian citizen. Simplest corporate entry</li><li><strong>Conversion:</strong> Voluntary to Pvt Ltd anytime via INC-6. No 2-year wait. Before fundraising</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
